<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6. </span>Runtime, Model Size, and Distillation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We measure efficiency on a single NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 Ti (11 GB). With 50 denoising steps, ReactDiff reaches 10.4 FPS. Reducing to 10 steps yields 36.9 FPS with a modest trade-off in FRDiv/FRCorr. After model distillation (83.95M <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 19.87M params), the 10-step model peaks at 42.3 FPS while remaining competitive on quality metrics (Tab. <a href="#A3.T16" title="Table 16 ‣ C.6. Runtime, Model Size, and Distillation ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ ReactDiff: Fundamental Multiple Appropriate Facial Reaction Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T16" class="ltx_table">
